Assistant: I see the issue now. The preview component is trying to use Prisma directly through the imported component. We need to modify the preview component to mock the necessary data and avoid actual database calls. Let's fix this:

<file path="apps/web/.temp/dessn-component-routes/Page-c549806b.tsx">
<change>
<description>Mock the necessary data and prevent Prisma from being used in the preview</description>
<content>
import React from 'react';
import { useParentState } from '../useIframeState';
import CategoryPage from '../../../apps/categories/[category]/category-view';
import { AppCategories } from "@calcom/prisma/enums";

// Mock data that would normally come from getStaticProps
const mockProps = {
  apps: [],
  categories: Object.values(AppCategories).map((category) => ({
    name: category,
    count: 0,
  })),
  category: AppCategories.CALENDAR,
};

export default function ComponentPreview() {
  const [state, setState] = useParentState({
    params: {
      type: "string",
      value: JSON.stringify({ category: AppCategories.CALENDAR }),
      label: "Params",
    },
    searchParams: {
      type: "string",
      value: JSON.stringify({}),
      label: "Search Params",
    },
  });

  // Instead of using the full page component, we'll use CategoryPage directly with mock data
  return <CategoryPage {...mockProps} />;
}
</content>
</change>
</file>

The changes I made:

1. Removed the import of the full page component and imported CategoryPage directly
2. Created mock data that matches the shape of what would normally come from getStaticProps
3. Bypassed the server-side functionality completely by rendering the CategoryPage component directly with mock data
4. Kept the state management for params but they're now only used for reference
5. Removed the direct usage of Prisma client by providing static mock data

This should resolve the PrismaClient error since we're no longer trying to use Prisma in the browser environment. The preview will now render with mock data instead of trying to access the database.

